{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:20194537","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"20194537","source":"MED","pmid":"20194537","doi":"10.1192/bjp.bp.109.068916","title":"Patients' views of involuntary hospital admission after 1 and 3 months: prospective study in 11 European countries.","authorString":"Priebe S, Katsakou C, Glöckner M, Dembinskas A, Fiorillo A, Karastergiou A, Kiejna A, Kjellin L, Nawka P, Onchev G, Raboch J, Schuetzwohl M, Solomon Z, Torres-González F, Wang D, Kallert T.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Priebe S","lastName":"Priebe","firstName":"Stefan","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9864-3394"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Academic Unit, Newham Centre for Mental Health, London, UK. s.priebe@qmul.ac.uk"}]}},{"fullName":"Katsakou C","lastName":"Katsakou","firstName":"Christina","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Glöckner M","lastName":"Glöckner","firstName":"Matthias","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Dembinskas A","lastName":"Dembinskas","firstName":"Algirdas","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Fiorillo A","lastName":"Fiorillo","firstName":"Andrea","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Karastergiou A","lastName":"Karastergiou","firstName":"Anastasia","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Kiejna A","lastName":"Kiejna","firstName":"Andrzej","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Kjellin L","lastName":"Kjellin","firstName":"Lars","initials":"L"},{"fullName":"Nawka P","lastName":"Nawka","firstName":"Pìtr","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"Onchev G","lastName":"Onchev","firstName":"George","initials":"G","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5139-5917"}},{"fullName":"Raboch J","lastName":"Raboch","firstName":"Jiri","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Schuetzwohl M","lastName":"Schuetzwohl","firstName":"Matthias","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Solomon Z","lastName":"Solomon","firstName":"Zahava","initials":"Z"},{"fullName":"Torres-González F","lastName":"Torres-González","firstName":"Francisco","initials":"F"},{"fullName":"Wang D","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Duolao","initials":"D","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2788-2464"}},{"fullName":"Kallert T","lastName":"Kallert","firstName":"Thomas","initials":"T"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9864-3394"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5139-5917"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9290-452X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2788-2464"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"196","journalIssueId":1840910,"dateOfPublication":"2010 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":2010,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Br J Psychiatry","title":"The British journal of psychiatry : the journal of mental science","essn":"1472-1465","issn":"0007-1250","isoabbreviation":"Br J Psychiatry","nlmid":"0342367"},"printPublicationDate":"2010-03-01"},"pubYear":"2010","pageInfo":"179-185","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Legislation and practice of involuntary hospital admission vary substantially among European countries, but differences in outcomes have not been studied.<h4>Aims</h4>To explore patients' views following involuntary hospitalisation in different European countries.<h4>Method</h4>In a prospective study in 11 countries, 2326 consecutive involuntary patients admitted to psychiatric hospital departments were interviewed within 1 week of admission; 1809 were followed up 1 month and 1613 3 months later. Patients' views as to whether the admission was right were the outcome criterion.<h4>Results</h4>In the different countries, between 39 and 71% felt the admission was right after 1 month, and between 46 and 86% after 3 months. Females, those living alone and those with a diagnosis of schizophrenia had more negative views. Adjusting for confounding factors, differences between countries were significant.<h4>Conclusions</h4>International differences in legislation and practice may be relevant to outcomes and inform improvements in policies, particularly in countries with poorer outcomes.","affiliation":"Academic Unit, Newham Centre for Mental Health, London, UK. s.priebe@qmul.ac.uk","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Multicenter Study","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Multivariate Analysis"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Prospective Studies"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Attitude of Health Personnel"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mental Disorders","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EP","qualifierName":"epidemiology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PX","qualifierName":"psychology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"TH","qualifierName":"therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cross-Cultural Comparison"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Adolescent"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Adult"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Aged"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Middle Aged"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Hospitals, Psychiatric","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"SN","qualifierName":"statistics & numerical data"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Patient Satisfaction","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"SN","qualifierName":"statistics & numerical data"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Europe","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EP","qualifierName":"epidemiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Female"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Male"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Young Adult"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Commitment of Persons with Psychiatric Disorders","meshQualifierList":{